Overview
As a culminating step in your learning journey, you will reflect on the experiences, challenges, and achievements you encountered throughout the course. Reflective writing is a powerful tool for consolidating learning and deepening self-awareness. This journal assignment gives you the opportunity to articulate what you have learned, evaluate how you have grown, and consider how you will apply your skills and insights in academic, professional, or personal contexts.

Whether you're heading into graduate research, working with stakeholders to make data-informed decisions, or developing visual content for a presentation, the ability to assess your growth and articulate what you’ve learned will support you well beyond this course. This journal helps you practice that skill, creating a record of learning that you can use to guide portfolio development, job interviews, or future projects.

Directions
In this journal assignment, you’ll evaluate how your knowledge and skills have developed throughout the course. You'll analyze specific challenges you faced, explain key decisions you made in creating your visualizations, and describe important insights you gained about data analysis and presentation.

Specifically, you must address the following rubric criteria:

Describe the most challenging aspect of the coursework and how you overcame it.
Explain how you plan to apply a specific data literacy skill in a future academic or professional context.
Evaluate how your use of data visualizations supported a data-driven narrative in one of your course assignments.
Describe how your perspective on working with data has changed since the beginning of the course.
